# Rover 200 SD3 (213/216), 1984-1989.
#
# The first Rover 200 was the second product of the BL-Honda alliance and a
# British-built Honda Ballade: a four-door notchback saloon, never a hatchback,
# launched on 19 June 1984 and sold as the 213 (Honda 1342 cc) and, from 1985, the
# 216 (BL S-series 1.6). It was pitched above the Maestro and Montego and became
# the quality benchmark of the Austin Rover range; sales peaked in 1988-89.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_200_/_25
# https://rover200.org.uk/cars/sd3
# https://www.aronline.co.uk/cars/rover/rover-213-216/unsung-heroes-rover-213216/
#
# Dimensions 4.156 x 1.623 x 1.378 m, wheelbase 2.450 m. Three independent sources
# agree on all four figures (Rover 200 & 400 Owners Club, carspecsguru, and the
# German Wikipedia dimension box).
#
# The 1987 update redesigned the rear lamp clusters and lowered the boot sill, and
# revised the interior. At 128 px that is a colour-run difference, not a second
# shell, so the pre-1987 rear is modelled for the whole run.
#
# Colours: Targa Red (BLVC 641), Silver Leaf metallic (421), Zircon Blue metallic
# (471) and Arum White (449), from the 1985 Rover 213 colour and trim chart.
# DVSA first-registration shares begin at 1994, so the split is era-adjusted from
# the 1994-96 measured base: red 6, silver 5, blue 4, white 3. Total 18.
# Provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 165 km/h, between the Maestro and the Rover 25's tier; the 216 EFi was the
# quick version. Comfort 85/310, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 85, at the Triumph 2000
# and Range Rover tier: the SD3 was bought for its refinement and the contemporary
# road tests made that its selling point. Classes 1,2, since it was priced above
# the mainstream.
#
# Dates are road presence, not production: June 1984 intro, retires staggered
# 1997-2000 on a thirteen- to sixteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-200-sd3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-200-sd3.dae (56 objects). References:
# citycars/references/rover-200-sd3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 2.0
# and CC BY 3.0).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: angular surfaces
# stand in for the photographed rounded corners, and the camera matching in the
# Gate B comparisons is approximate rather than calibrated.

obj=citycar
name=Rover200SD3(TargaRed)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=6
intro_year=1984
intro_month=6
retire_year=1998
retire_month=6
speed=165
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=85
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=310

